{"base_rate":0.5258152173913043,"brier":0.2593490489130435,"bss":-0.040168975959367303,"bss_hi":0.048266004001777635,"bss_lo":-0.15033247681786338,"chart":{"base":[516.5,258.0],"fp":[62.0,128.3],"lead":"62,250.9 272,244.4 482,241.5 692,209.7","note":{"base":"skill -0.04 — higher than 10% of cities","fp":"low end -11pp, high end +28pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 48% of cities","rel":"promised 37% → rained 13%; promised 99% → rained 76%"},"rel":"292.2,407.8 514.5,327.8 616.9,202.2 683.5,135.8"},"country":"SG","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.26822010869565216,"ess":439.223625491161,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Singapore</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Singapore rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 8 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>79%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(23%), there is still roughly a <b>8%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 736 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 17.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.04, ranked 195 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(184&ndash;203) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>23%</td><td class='num'><b>8%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>51%</td><td class='num'><b>19%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>67%</td><td class='num'><b>26%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>77%</td><td class='num'><b>38%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>85%</td><td class='num'><b>56%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>91%</td><td class='num'><b>68%</b></td><td class='num'>59</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>95%</td><td class='num'><b>69%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>79%</b></td><td class='num'>242</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">8 of 8 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Singapore</b> <span class=\"muted\">Singapore</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;53% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 53% of days.</p><p>The forecast did worse than that guess. The difference is within the margin of error.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">8 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>-0.04</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>184&ndash;203\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>736 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Singapore &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Singapore\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"138.7895890410959,262.32876712328766 239.52911764705883,151.82352941176472 294.07662337662333,103.09090909090907 331.50136986301374,67.86301369863014 360.375,43.27777777777777 381.34,24.169491525423723 395.5291666666666,18.0 410.66884297520664,18.0 410.66884297520664,22.512396694214885 395.5291666666666,53.38888888888886 381.34,79.69491525423729 360.375,103.94444444444446 331.50136986301374,137.6712328767123 294.07662337662333,178.72727272727275 239.52911764705883,237.47058823529412 138.7895890410959,332.13698630136986\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"190.60326086956522\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"190.60326086956522\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"138.7895890410959,352.0821917808219 239.52911764705883,312.4117647058824 294.07662337662333,287.4545454545455 331.50136986301374,242.38356164383563 360.375,179.77777777777777 381.34,135.22033898305085 395.5291666666666,129.22222222222223 410.66884297520664,96.2148760330578\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 23%&amp;#10;It rained 8% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"138.7895890410959\" cy=\"352.0821917808219\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 51%&amp;#10;It rained 19% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"239.52911764705883\" cy=\"312.4117647058824\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 67%&amp;#10;It rained 26% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"294.07662337662333\" cy=\"287.4545454545455\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 77%&amp;#10;It rained 38% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"331.50136986301374\" cy=\"242.38356164383563\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 85%&amp;#10;It rained 56% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"360.375\" cy=\"179.77777777777777\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 91%&amp;#10;It rained 68% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 59 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"381.34\" cy=\"135.22033898305085\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 95%&amp;#10;It rained 69% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"395.5291666666666\" cy=\"129.22222222222223\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 79% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 242 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.66884297520664\" cy=\"96.2148760330578\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(53%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Singapore the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.16) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.30).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>182</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>-0.296</td><td class='num'>34.3%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>178</td><td class='num'>57%</td><td class='num'>-0.123</td><td class='num'>26.7%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>172</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>-0.101</td><td class='num'>31.8%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>204</td><td class='num'>67%</td><td class='num'>0.163</td><td class='num'>16.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":1.28967,"lon":103.85007,"n":736,"n_cities":216,"name":"Singapore","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.41,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.22821917808219178,"n":73,"obs":0.0821917808219178,"sig":true},{"hi":0.61,"lo":0.41,"mean":0.5127941176470588,"n":68,"obs":0.19117647058823528,"sig":true},{"hi":0.74,"lo":0.61,"mean":0.66688311